      "hints": [
        "Factorise $(2\\cos 2x + 1)(\\cos 2x + 1) = 0 \\implies \\cos 2x = -\\frac{1}{2}, -1$.",
        "Solve in $[0^\\circ, 180^\\circ]$ to find $x = 60^\\circ, 90^\\circ, 120^\\circ$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Factorise the quadratic equation in $\\cos(2x)$:\n$$(2\\cos(2x) + 1)(\\cos(2x) + 1) = 0$$\n$$\\cos(2x) = -\\frac{1}{2} \\quad \\text{or} \\quad \\cos(2x) = -1$$",
        "Solve for $2x$ in the interval $0^\\circ \\le 2x \\le 360^\\circ$ (for $0^\\circ \\le x \\le 180^\\circ$):\n$$\\text{For } \\cos(2x) = -\\frac{1}{2}: \\quad 2x = 120^\\circ, \\quad 240^\\circ \\implies x = 60^\\circ, \\quad 120^\\circ$$\n$$\\text{For } \\cos(2x) = -1: \\quad 2x = 180^\\circ \\implies x = 90^\\circ$$\n$$(\\text{Solutions: } x = 60^\\circ, \\quad 90^\\circ, \\quad 120^\\circ)$$"
      ],
